/**
 * @page UseCase Rainwater Buffering Use Case
 *
 * @brief Monitoring household rainwater storage in the Municipality of Apeldoorn.
 *
 * @section Background Background
 *
 * Due to climate change, periods of drought are increasingly
 * alternating with heavy rainfall. During intense rain showers,
 * large amounts of water enter the sewer system, which can lead
 * to flooding and damage. To reduce this pressure, the Municipality
 * of Apeldoorn encourages residents to disconnect roof drainage
 * from the sewer and collect rainwater locally.
 *
 * @section Goal Goal
 *
 * The municipality would like to determine the effectiveness of
 * disconnecting roof drainage from the sewer system by measuring:
 *
 * - How much rainwater is stored.
 * - How much water is used.
 * - Over what period the stored water is returned to the environment.
 *
 * @section Solution Solution
 *
 * This project implements a LoRaWAN-based monitoring node for a
 * rainwater barrel. The node measures:
 *
 * - Water level.
 * - Water consumption.
 * - Battery condition.
 *
 * The measurements are transmitted through the LoRaWAN network
 * for further analysis.
 *
 * @section Prototype Prototype
 *
 * During development, physical sensors are emulated using
 * potentiometers and a push button. This allows the complete
 * measurement and communication chain to be validated before
 * deploying real sensors.
 *
 * @see ShieldLayout
 * @see ApplicationArchitecture
 */